<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20882] contrib: checkpatch-man.pl and commit-msg hook problems on Debian/Ubuntu</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20882</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Two small problems in contrib scripts, both seen on Ubuntu hosts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. contrib/scripts/checkpatch-man.pl looks up the release that added a man page's subject with a git log/awk pipeline run through Perl backticks, i.e. /bin/sh. The pipeline uses a bash here-string (&amp;lt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt;). Where /bin/sh is dash (Debian, Ubuntu) every lookup fails with:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  Doing long search for AVAILABILITY version: git log -S '&amp;lt;subject&amp;gt;'&lt;br/&gt;
  sh: 1: Syntax error: redirection unexpected&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;and checkpatch reports "no git commit hash found", so the AVAILABILITY suggestion never works there.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. contrib/git-hooks/commit-msg --help creates its temporary message file with mktemp "$ORIGINAL.XXXXXX" even though there is no message file, so it leaves a stray file in the current directory and never removes it: a hidden .XXXXXX file with GNU coreutils, a visible untracked XXXXXX file with uutils coreutils (Ubuntu 26.04's default). --help also prints "basename: missing operand".&lt;/p&gt;</description>
